;;; An hrule's `:assert (absent (paid ?g))` splits R on a fact nothing reads —
;;; M1f **W80**, register row `W80/absent-hrule-concluded`, filed by S1f.7.7 (T1f.7.7.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests and an hrule that proposes `(absent (paid ?g))` of each.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; No conclusion is headed `absent`, an hrule's neither: refused at the parse, on every
;;; command.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `52e05fc1`, release: the program loads; H is `(absent (paid Ann))` and
;;; `(absent (paid Bob))`, and R is four states that differ only in facts of `absent`,
;;; which no premise can read: the goal has no row in any, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.7 (T1f.7.7.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(hrule guess () :match (is-a ?g Guest) :assert (absent (paid ?g)) :why "suppose {?g} has not paid")
(query :goal (paid ?g))
